PLACEHOLDER: demucs_v4_quantized.onnx is currently NOT exportable.

Status: blocked_export

Why:
  HDemucs (the architecture behind every demucs v4 variant including
  htdemucs, mdx, mdx_extra, mdx_q) uses an internal torch.stft on
  complex tensors. PyTorch's torch.onnx.export at opset 17 fails with
  SymbolicValueError("STFT does not currently support complex types").
  Opset 20 traces the graph but emits an OOM during graph emission on
  hosts with <8 GB free disk, and even on completion the resulting ONNX
  is >300 MB after quantization. There is no pure-waveform demucs
  variant in the 4.x line. mdx_extra is shipped as a BagOfModels
  ensemble (4 sub-models); the export wrapper unwraps to bag.models[0]
  for traceability, but this still does not bypass the STFT blocker.

How to unblock:
  1. Wait for torch.onnx.dynamo_export to support complex-tensor STFT,
     OR
  2. Patch demucs/hdemucs.py to replace torch.stft with a custom layer
     that splits real and imaginary parts before the FFT op,
     OR
  3. Fine-tune a published waveform-only separator (e.g. Wave-U-Net,
     Spleeter-2-stem) and ship that under this filename.

Until then ml-worker.js detects the missing file and runs the DSP-only
path. Audio still processes at full quality minus the Demucs stem.
